WEBVTT

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.850
Kaito?!

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.360
Raetsel!

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.460
So she’s Raetsel?

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.190
What are you up to?

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.880
Rook! Freecell!

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.430
It’s freaking rare to 
see those two team up!

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.380
Sure is... Hey, this isn’t 
the time for mindless chitchat!

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.900
Kaito, where exactly 
are you at the moment?

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.260
Inside of a Mayan pyramid.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.320
In order to solve a puzzle, we’re 
currently in a pyramid in Egypt.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.820
You’re in a pyramid, too?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.870
Two pyramids... two puzzles...

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.020
Figured it out?

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.000
That’s right. I contrived 
this whole thing.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:30.000
If It Were The Us of Then

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.980
The Mayan pyramid and 
the Egyptian pyramid...

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.510
These two puzzles are interlinked.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:44.130
Rook, when I heard that you were going 
to investigate that Egyptian pyramid,

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.860
a light bulb went on.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:50.910
First I needed to lure Kaito Daimon 
here, to this Mayan pyramid.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.400
Then I could trap all of you 
inside of the two pyramids...

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.250
...for all eternity!

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.580
So I remade the puzzles.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:04.530
The ruins had been completely 
empty--devoid of any prizes!

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:09.410
But I cranked up the difficulty level 
and made Kaito Daimon the prize!

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.020
They were empty?

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.930
I can’t believe you pulled 
that Jin wannabe card on us!

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.920
That was a low!

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.930
You’ve rounded up all of the 
Phi-Brain children using these puzzles?

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.490
How splendid!

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:29.360
Raetsel, I was right to sign that 
contract with you after all.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:35.070
Rook and Freecell... Their 
natural strengths lie as Givers.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:40.880
I wonder how long they will last 
in Raetsel’s puzzle as Solvers.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:47.460
You think this pyramid is empty?

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.040
Raetsel, you don’t know anything.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.790
Not about us or this puzzle!

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.720
We will solve this puzzle,

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.230
free Kaito and his friends 
and obtain the hidden prize!

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.100
Allow us to show you what the Phi-Brain 
children are truly made of!

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.650
Rook!

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:12.060
He can talk the talk!

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.240
Are you ready, Mr. Freecell?

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.320
Whenever you are, Mr. Rook!

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:27.670
“Hidden treasure”? 
What’s he talking about?

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:29.950
I’m going to explain the rules.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:33.210
You two must simultaneously 
solve this maze,

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.060
which runs through those ruins.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:40.270
Notice how there are emblems 
of gods engraved on the walls?

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:43.680
This?

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:50.940
Amun, Atum, Geb, Horus, 
Osiris, Ra and Shu.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:52.990
If you touch an emblem,

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.030
it will make a wall with 
another emblem move.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.850
This will allow you to move forward.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.440
Take turns raising the walls to proceed.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:22.690
If you manage to reach the 
center of the maze, you win!

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.200
I see...

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.470
That’s why we’re at 
different starting points.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.520
You have a total of 10 minutes.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:33.280
If you exceed the allotted time, 
all of the doors will seal shut.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:37.060
You’ll never get to see the 
light of day... ever again.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.040
I went all out when I made this puzzle.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.480
So you had better brace yourselves!

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.200
Mr. Freecell, let’s start 
by looking for the emblems.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.650
Sounds good. We need to 
identify the principles

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.620
behind the emblems and their layout.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:56.500
Horus!

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.200
The key to lifting Geb is Shu!

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:22.270
Got it!

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.160
I’m going to touch Osiris.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.050
Horus just went up!

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:47.670
The emblems are connected 
in order of Atum, Shu, Geb,

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:51.920
Osiris, Horus, Amun and Ra!

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.680
If we get stuck,

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.510
we simply need to search for 
whatever emblem raises that wall.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.270
We only have so much time!

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:03.520
Let’s take the shortest 
route possible!

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.040
Sounds good!

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.270
Most impressive!

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.950
They managed to quickly identify the 
correlation between the emblems.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.750
Next up is Atum!

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:25.290
This one should be connected 
with part of the upcoming maze.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:26.550
So I should hit this one!

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:46.800
I swear I will free this puzzle!

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:51.570
I will save Kaito, obtain the prize 
and release Jin’s memories!

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:12.050
As expected from Mr. Rook, he’s fast!

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:15.050
Are you there yet, Mr. Freecell?

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.340
If Mr. Rook ups the speed another 
notch, I won’t be able to keep up!

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:55.840
Next I need an Amun!

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:58.500
Is Amun here?!

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:07.680
Amun isn’t here either!

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.960
Is Amun over here?!

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.100
What an odd place to 
put an Osiris emblem...

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:36.260
Is there a problem, Mr. Freecell?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:39.140
No, it’s nothing.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.020
Next I need a Shu!

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.150
Mr. Freecell!

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:01.890
B-believe it or not, I can’t 
find a Shu emblem anywhere!

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:03.380
What?

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.190
What’s going on?

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:09.420
Why can’t we move forward?

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:11.930
It doesn’t matter how hard you think.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:17.050
You’ll never be able 
to solve this puzzle.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.930
It can’t be...! There 
isn’t an answer?!

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:21.490
Didn’t I warn you?

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:26.290
This puzzle is meant to keep 
you trapped for all eternity.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:36.240
This is for the best, isn’t it, Jin?

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:39.200
What should I do?

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:43.260
How can I...? How should 
I tackle this puzzle?

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:44.880
This could be it for us...

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:48.590
Mr. Freecell, how could you...?!

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:52.330
As Solvers, we’ve made it as 
far as we can in this puzzle.

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:58.710
But as Givers, we might 
be able to keep at it.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:10:59.800
What?

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:04.690
I have personally created a puzzle 
that was meant to trap someone

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.400
so he could never, ever leave.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.760
If it were the us of back then...

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:16.540
We could understand this puzzle 
and find a way to solve it.

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:19.780
You’re amazing, Mr. Freecell.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.270
Let’s do it!

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:25.420
Let’s remember what 
we were like back then!

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:32.800
They’re retracing their steps?!

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.920
There ain’t time for that!

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:37.420
What are they up to?

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.900
What would I do if I wanted to 
trap my opponents in this puzzle?

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.390
What would I do to keep 
them from ever leaving?

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:49.640
I should be able to 
understand this puzzle!

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:54.730
I put my heart into a puzzle and 
tried to become immortal to Kaito.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:01.970
I put my heart into a puzzle and tried 
to spend all of eternity with Kaito.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:05.610
I’m confident we can understand 
this puzzle because of who we are!

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:08.990
Isn’t this...?

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:11.040
It stood out to me earlier...

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:14.460
There were two walls with Amun near 
each other that felt strange...

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:19.850
If it were me, I would make the 
other Amun lead to a dead end

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:21.190
to catch Kaito.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:26.460
In order to keep Kaito from 
escaping, I would do the same.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:29.770
This is where we made our mistake!

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.770
This is where we’ll start over!

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:42.330
It’s puzzle time... Let’s start!

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:53.960
Rook...

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.650
Freecell...

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:59.270
When we went all out and

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:01.550
made our own perfect puzzles 
that had no answers,

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:04.060
Kaito was able to solve them.

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:08.480
I’m sure this must have one!

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.220
Somewhere, Raetsel put 
a tear in her puzzle!

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:14.690
There isn’t an Atum!

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:16.730
Hit a dead end?

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:24.450
But it doesn’t match 
prior placement patterns!

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.320
This just might be...

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:28.810
...Raetsel’s tear!

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:30.720
I found it!

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:33.420
Are you all set, Mr. Rook?

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.710
Whenever you are, Mr. Freecell.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:42.340
Let’s do it!

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:55.270
Now!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.210
They’re taking advantage of

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.530
the split second when 
both walls are going up?!

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:07.670
Go!

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:23.700
We solved it...!

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:31.300
Way to go, Rook and Freecell!

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:34.810
I had no idea they could 
solve it like that...

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.560
This was an incredible puzzle!

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:40.730
It was a strong, strict and fair puzzle.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.690
It reminds me of Kaito.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:47.420
Even though it was meant to 
trap us for all eternity,

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:48.650
this puzzle still had an answer.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.820
It may have been done subconsciously,

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:54.530
but you made sure that this 
puzzle could be solved.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:15:00.830
As a result, we were able to understand 
this puzzle as Givers and solve it.

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:03.710
What the heck are they talking about?!

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.980
They’re saying that you’ve lost.

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:09.220
You should pull back.

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:13.690
A mere teen could not hope to mend 
the situation as things stand.

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:18.950
But... I’m not gonna give up!

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:23.480
Wait, Raetsel! Where is Jin?!

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.730
It’s just as I had feared.

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:31.800
Despite her talk of “determination,” 
Raetsel’s subconscious kindness kicked in...

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:34.990
To think that would get in the way.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.950
Damn those Phi-Brain children!

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.220
Wh-what?!

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:47.130
Crap! It’s gonna collapse!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.260
Found it!

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:55.820
Mr. Rook, what is that?

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:58.860
Supposedly the hidden 
prize will only appear if

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:00.900
the two switches are 
pressed simultaneously.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.350
But I only see one!

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:06.860
Wait, Mr. Rook! There 
are two switches...

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:09.110
And two pyramids...

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:10.830
And two puzzles!

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:12.240
Kaito!

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:16.300
Please search that room for anything 
that could pass as a switch!

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:17.950
A switch?

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:21.430
I, Ana, think this is it!

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:23.460
I found it, Rook!

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:26.470
I’m counting down from 
five! Push it when I do!

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:27.460
Sure thing!

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:28.640
Here I go!

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:29.600
Five...

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:30.560
Four...

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:31.690
Three...

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:32.810
Two...

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:33.340
One...

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:34.610
Zero!

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:49.070
It’s...!

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:51.490
It’s the Pythagoras Document!

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:59.030
It contains the secrets 
regarding the Puzzle of God

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.750
left behind by the 
philosopher Pythagoras.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:07.090
So these two puzzles were connected 
in order to seal off these prizes?

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:09.130
Let’s get out of here!

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:14.630
Thanks a bunch, Rook! Freecell!

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:18.280
I swear I’ll get this to 
the POG’s headquarters.

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:19.220
Right!

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:20.780
Hurry!

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:23.360
Nonoha, fight!

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:25.820
I’m stuck being the mule again?!

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.260
We made it out in one piece!

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:42.330
Thank you, Mr. Freecell.

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:46.420
Thanks to you, we were able to 
get the Pythagoras Document.

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:49.450
No, it was all thanks to you, Mr. Rook.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:50.910
Rook...

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:54.300
It’s okay. You may call me Rook.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:59.140
Then you’re welcome 
to call me Freecell.

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:02.060
Hey!

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.060
Freecell!

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.700
Master Rook!

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:11.510
Director Rook did a

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:15.320
splendid job retrieving the 
Pythagoras Document, didn’t he?

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:18.670
You’ve done well. 
I never expected you

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:21.830
to get your hands on this 
classified information.

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:23.430
It was nothing!

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:28.010
The apple pie in the Republic 
of Amgine was delicious.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:32.420
President Johan Sigmund Enigma...

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:37.310
How could someone bent on wiping 
puzzlers off the face of the planet

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:43.350
know so much about Jin Makata’s 
past and the Puzzle of God?

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:47.320
Not to mention the ancient 
Philosopher’s Puzzle.

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:53.980
Even Director Rook didn’t know the 
scale of the puzzle, so how did he?

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:58.680
If he used to serve as that 
puzzle’s administrator,

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:00.990
it would explain a great deal.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:04.380
All of the pieces are 
coming together now.

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:08.480
So it was you...?

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:22.150
Jin...

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:30.720
Jin, I just got back!

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:34.540
What’s the matter, Jin?

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:36.640
I don’t have a can opener...

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:40.490
How can I open this without one...?

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:43.290
It’s a challenging puzzle...

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:48.680
Jin! Hey! Hang in there!

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:52.650
Man, that was a close call!

00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:58.520
Sheesh! You’re so stupid!

00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:01.230
Couldn’t you have gone out 
and bought a can opener?

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:05.060
I don’t know anything about this town.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:10.010
Plus you specifically asked me to 
stay here and hold down the fort.

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.770
So you stayed here this whole 
time and waited for me?

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.860
Thank you, Jin.

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:21.500
Eat all you want!

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:30.130
They solved the best 
puzzle I could think up.

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:37.210
At this rate, it’s 
just a matter of time...

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:41.940
It’s okay! I haven’t lost yet.

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:44.590
We’ll hang low in 
this town for a while.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:48.600
Are you sure that’s wise?

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:53.920
Huh?

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:55.830
I’ve been debating.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:58.130
You or Kaito?

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:01.810
Between the two of you, 
who do I truly need?

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:07.160
What are you talking about, Jin?

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:16.460
Enigma!

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:20.680
What do you want at this hour?

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:22.900
We’ve got an emergency, Raetsel!

00:21:23.270 --> 00:21:27.400
It looks like the POG have 
sniffed out your hideout!

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:30.190
They should be there at any minute!

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:35.770
If you don’t want them 
to steal your beloved Jin,

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:37.110
get out of there this instant!

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:48.200
Well then, I might as 
well inform the POG...

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.290
...where their hideout is.

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:56.100
Raetsel, you will never 
find a moment’s respite.

00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:00.280
A cat becomes fierce, 
even vicious, after it

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:03.580
has been chased, hunted, 
and driven into a corner.

00:22:04.400 --> 00:22:09.220
You must grow stronger if you are 
to defeat the Phi-Brain children.

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:13.470
Isn’t that right, Lovushka?

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:20.380
I don’t have any other choice...

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:25.710
I’ll have to risk my life in 
a battle with Kaito Daimon...!

00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:05.770
You’re the culprit, aren’t 
you? Well, Upperclassman Jikukawa?

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:07.690
No, it wasn’t me!

00:24:07.690 --> 00:24:10.310
Can you still say that 
after seeing this?

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:12.820
That’s my apple juice!

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:14.420
I found it at the scene of the crime.

00:24:16.150 --> 00:24:18.180
It... was me.

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:22.100
Next time, “I Want to Make 
a World with Full Bellies.”

00:24:19.330 --> 00:24:27.980
I Want to Make a World with Full Bellies

00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:27.200
I ate all of the apple pies 
that I bought as souvenirs!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Aren’t you getting carried away?
 But they’re so good!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
